Coopr corresponding source

This archive accompanies the Linux binaries and container image in the same release.
coopr/ contains the application source and its build definitions.
vendor/ contains the Go dependencies used for that build, including their
license files. sources/ holds each shared upstream source once.
libraries/ links to the sources for statically linked native libraries,
with their applied patches in series order. container/ links to the
sources supplied for shipped runtime packages and their applied patches.
Its patch inventories describe the @hostSystem@ build;
platform-specific patches for other targets are in the pinned Nixpkgs tree.
Relative links work outside the Nix store. GCC sources are included for
its distributed runtime libraries; general build tools such as the Go
compiler are obtained through Nix rather than bundled here.
build-inputs/ contains the pinned Nix inputs, including Nixpkgs' package
recipes and local patches. Fetched patches accompany their source packages.
Permissively licensed Netavark and Aardvark Rust sources are not bundled;
their recursive license and copyright notices remain in the image.

With Nix installed, rebuild the original application from this directory:

  nix build path:./coopr#coopr-static
  ./result/bin/coopr --help

Rebuild the container using the same pinned package recipes:

  nix build path:./coopr#container-archive

To modify a container runtime dependency, override its source in the
Nixpkgs input. Its original source is bundled under container/. The
pinned Nixpkgs tree under build-inputs/ contains its build recipe; fetched
patches are alongside its source under container/.

Nix fetches the versions recorded in coopr/flake.lock and go.mod/go.sum.
It may need network access to obtain the compiler and other build tools.

To rebuild with a modified library, unpack its archive, make your changes,
and override that library's src in coopr/nix/package-static.nix. For example,
run the following from the archive root:

  tar -xf libraries/gpgme/*.tar.bz2 -C coopr

Add this attribute to the existing gpgme.overrideAttrs block in
coopr/nix/package-static.nix, using your extracted directory name:

  src = ../gpgme-@gpgmeVersion@;

Re-run the nix build command. Nix rebuilds GPGME and relinks Coopr against
the modified library. Other linked libraries can likewise be overridden
through pkgs.pkgsStatic.callPackage's arguments or its stdenv for musl.

To use the bundled Go dependency sources, copy vendor/ to coopr/vendor/,
include ../vendor in the fileset in coopr/nix/package.nix, and set
vendorHash = null in that file. Go then builds with those vendored sources.

The original Nix input source trees can be extracted from build-inputs/.
Use nix build's --override-input option to select modified local input
trees instead of the locked remote inputs, such as a modified Nixpkgs.

Coopr's MIT license does not replace the licenses of its dependencies.
See the notices shipped with the binary and the licenses in these sources.
No additional restrictions apply to modifying the LGPL libraries or reverse
engineering Coopr to debug those modifications.
